	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (powerboard connector J1)\nEach rail: polyfuse -> P-FET reverse-polarity -> TVS, emerging as +5V_PB / +3V3_PB.\nQ1/Q2 orientation: DRAIN->input, SOURCE->load, GATE->GND via 100k (R43/R44).\nA reversed supply reverse-biases the body diode AND drives Vgs to 0 => blocked.\nEach TVS sits AFTER its FET, so it never sees a reversed input."
		(at 33.02 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4b234d6-9f6b-44c6-94be-3a4297bbbc84")
	)
	(text "POWER MUX - powerboard has priority over USB.\nTPS2116 MODE tied to VIN1 = priority mode (TI SLVSFG1A sec 7.6.1); VREF(PR1) = 1.0V typ.\n  U1 (5V):   VIN1 = +5V_PB,  VIN2 = VBUS.       PR1 divider 100k/33k -> switchover at 4.03V\n  U2 (3V3):  VIN1 = +3V3_PB, VIN2 = +3V3_LDO.   PR1 divider 100k/68k -> switchover at 2.47V\nWith the powerboard present, PR1 > VREF so VIN1 (powerboard) is selected. With USB only,\n+5V_PB/+3V3_PB = 0V so PR1 < VREF and the mux falls back to VBUS / the LDO.\n\nCAUTION - USB-only operation is for BENCH PROGRAMMING, not full operation:\nU3 (TLV1117-33) is 800 mA and dissipates (5.0-3.3) x I = 1.4 W at 800 mA.\nThe radio module alone draws 650 mA on +3V3, plus ~330 mA on +5V for LEDs/OLED.\nThat exceeds both a default USB port and U3's comfortable dissipation."
		(at 33.02 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ff126b98-59f6-47f4-99aa-aeb8e14b2cff")
	)
