  (text "LIMITS / DESIGN NOTES\n1. D9 TVS0500 is a FLAT CLAMP (6.0V), chosen because TPS2116 abs max VIN is 6.0V.\n   A plain SMAJ6.0A clamps at 10.3V and would NOT have protected the mux.\n2. D10 on the 3V3 rail is transient/ESD only. No flat-clamp part exists below 5V Vrwm,\n   and SMAJ4.0CA does not conduct until 4.44V while STM32 VDD abs max is 4.0V.\n   A SUSTAINED 3V3 overvoltage is therefore NOT protected; the polyfuse trips on\n   overcurrent only. Upgrade path: active OVP load switch (TPS2595 / NCP360) for F3/Q2.\n3. R4 = 68k, not 56k. The series drop lowers +3V3_PB, and a 100k/56k divider puts\n   V(PR1) at 1.077V against the TPS2116 1.08V max VREF at 2A, so the mux would falsely\n   declare the powerboard rail dead. 100k/68k restores margin.\n4. Series drop budget per rail: P-FET 70-100 mOhm + polyfuse ~50 mOhm."
    (at 33.02 232.41 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "38b69c0c-05fd-4845-8f03-f308cb11136c")
  )
